Before you start buying an electric vehicle, it is important to know about its operating mode, charging method and, in particular, about its annual consumption. The specialists of the IZI by EDF network will answer your questions about the electricity consumption of a car, the average cost of recharging, as well as changes in the battery capacity in the long term.
Electric vehicle consumption typically ranges from 12 to 15 kWh per 100 km. The average cost per kilowatt-hour of consumption of your electric vehicle depends on the tariff set by your electricity supplier.
The cost of recharging your car with electricity averages € 0,25 per kWh. This means that with an annual consumption of 1800 kWh, electricity consumption will be around 450 euros.
As well as the chosen model.
The more expensive it is to buy an electric car, the longer its battery life will be. For the most basic electric vehicles, you will only be able to drive 80 to 100 km, which is enough for everyday use when your work is near you.
The price per kilometer for an electric car is 3-4 times lower than that of an equivalent thermal model. However, to take advantage of this bargain price, it is important to subscribe to full off-peak hours with your electricity provider.
Vehicle power consumption per 100 km The cost of fully charging the battery * Average annual cost of electricity *
More on the topic:
In addition, there are now many facilities for recharging electric vehicles in cities. An important property is not to discharge the battery, especially on long trips.
In certain car parks of supermarkets, supermarkets and shopping centers;
Subscribing during off-peak and peak hours can be interesting as you can charge your electric vehicle during low-demand hours at a more attractive price. Then you can choose a fast charging cycle (6 hours on average).
While progress is needed to democratize electric vehicles, it avoids the use of fossil fuels such as diesel and gasoline. Thus, it has a great advantage over internal combustion vehicles.
If the initial investment is greater, its long-term consumption is much more economical.
