CDS(cold drawn steel) seamless tube and pipe is produced by piercing hot billets and subsequent rolling which reduces their diameter and elongates them. This material is then passed through a die and over a mandrel plug to produce an accurate size and gauge which is the essence of the cold drawing process.
Due to the superior strength and hardness, it produces a better machined surface and therefore a better-looking component.
As cold drawn tubes have a glossier, no-seam finish they also produce better end products from processes such as dipping, etching and anodizing.
Tokyo Steel Manufacturing, Japan’s leading electric-arc-furnace producer, announced on September 14 to keep all its carbon steel finished products prices unchanged for October sales, using the one month to review how much of its previous price hikes have been absorbed by the spot market and to monitor the steel market development both at home and abroad.
Meanwhile, the market is mixed with positive and negative news, Mysteel Global understood from Kiyoshi Imamura, Tokyo Steel’s managing director, as on the one hand, flats supply tightness has delayed the progress of some domestic construction projects, but the situation is improving with demand of construction steel expected to rise in the second half of FY21 (October-March 2022).
On the other hand, uncertainties still hover above the overseas steel market because of the new wave of the COVID-19, and steel demand in Southeast Asia, for example, has been dampened.
