From Concentration Camp to University Instructor: Enduring the harsh conditions in camp | Refugee Center Online | Refugee Center Online
Enduring harsh conditions in concentration camps, this refugee became a college Instructor.
Later, they greatly contributed to the development of this country.
Later they became university professors, scientists, diplomats or famous scholars.
Their voices should be heard to encourage others to take the same path.
I heard many great stories among them.
She later became a great university instructor.
Karaz, a Kurdish refugee from Iraq, came to the United States of America with her family many years ago.
Then they stayed in Syria for several years.
They stayed there for a long time without getting any basic services like health, education, housing and so.
Due to lack of proper medical treatments and clinical facilities, Karaz lost her small brother while they were in those camps.
Her education passion and curiosity pushed her to finish her GED certificate.
Great grades for the school and the family support encouraged her.
After several years, Karaz is now a university lecturer at the mentioned University.
Karaz told me that nothing can stop you from achieving your dreams once you strongly believed in those goals.
Karaz’s story is wonderful and inspiring for all refugees in this country.
This story tells us that when the opportunities are available, refugees can contribute a lot to this country.
