On September 30th, 2017, The Refugee Center Online together with UC Berkely Hass, School of Business hosted a resource hackathon conference to help build tools for refugees to build new lives in America.
What came out of the event was indeed satisfactory.
Each group had to come up with an idea that could help make the lives of refugees in America easier.
As groups began their ideas, they first had to learn about each other because everyone came from different organizations and locations.
I also shared how even when you make a significant in one person’s life.
The conference was full of love and laughter.
Of course, there were moments of silence where people were truly focused and did not want to be bothered.
What could have possibly made these individuals give up their whole Saturday to seat in a room full of strangers to build tools to help refugees in the United States?
Question: Why did you choose to participate at this event?
We have a lot of problems in Europe and I want to learn ways to solve a problem
I care for people in general.
I am an engineer so, this is also a way I can use my skills to make a difference.
And I feel like there is work that can be done to make that less stressful.
I just want to help and also become part of this and share my experiences.
