When was World Refugee Day started?
The first World Refugee Day was celebrated in 2001, in honor of the 50th anniversary of the 1951 Convention Related to the Status of Refugees (the legal document that protected refugees after World War II).
Many countries honor World Refugee Day by illuminating major landmarks.
