However, everyone have one thing in common: All of us have to start somewhere.
Though there are many paths to success, no one wants to take a long and tiring path.
Dream big and have the vision of what you want to achieve
If you walk in the darkness without a light, not only does it slow the process of getting where you wish to go, it also makes the whole process more difficult.
Do not be afraid to dream big.
Do not be afraid to make decisions.
If you live in the United States, you do have many opportunities.
Now, you are living in a developed country that allows you to dream as big as you want.
But where there is opportunity, there comes responsibility.
You are responsible for the life ahead of you.
Sometime it helps to write down your goals.
Often times, people will have an example of what it is they want to accomplish and let that serve as a reminder of what they want.
You can buy a small empty booklet at your local store and put it in your room to serve as a reminder of what it is you want to achieve.
Take action and work hard
You have to remind yourself that nothing is going to be done without taking actions to achieve it.
Working hard means you are doing something each and every day to get closer to your goal.
At times we must take a step back and ask ourselves: How is this helping me achieve my goals?
Why do I want what I want?
We all feel lazy at times.
Sometimes you get tired and feel like you are not doing good at all.
But the people who keep pushing through those times are the ones who are able to succeed.
You should never have to stop because you feel tired.
Do not ever think you are not doing good.
You have to keep on the great work!
Another thing you have to keep in mind is that life is a journey.
You have a vision of what you want to accomplish.
Well you cannot eat an elephant in one bite!
When you experience difficulties on your way to success.
And the only way you are going to eat it all is if you take smaller bites each and everyday.
In other words, when you take smaller actions each and everything, you will make a great progress and you will achieve your dream.
Take action and work hard.
Finally, remember that life is a journey.
To eat the elephant, you must chop it up into smaller pieces!
