He learned to ask for help, to stay late and put in extra time with his teachers.
Felix came at a younger age and says his transition to school in the United States was a bit easier.
Felix wants to help other refugee and immigrant students “take pride in their backgrounds and stories.”
Even though my mom doesn’t always understand my homework or the school system, she “Always encourages me,” said Abel.
Felix said, “One of the most important milestones for me was understanding just how much my parents went through to ensure I could get an education.
Today, Abel and Felix are both leaders in their community and school.
Abel has arranged two different school supply drives, collecting donated items for over 200 students.
Felix recently attending a sociology camp and Stanford University and this fall will be doing motivational speaking with refugee youth in elementary and middle schools.
“We want other students to be proud to say they are refugees.
