I have so many things in life to be thankful that I couldn’t even name or counted.
I remember my mom always told me that no matter how hard life is, even in the time that you think you have nothing to be thankful for, remember you are the greatest creation on earth and be thankful for that.
There is always something to be appreciated in life both in your best time or worst.
I thank God each day for my family, especially my parents.
My family is there for me wherever I needed them.
My parents worked so hard day by day to raise us and yet they never give up on us or complained.
They are the great example for me and they inspired me in so many different ways.
Having them and being able to call them my parents was the best thing ever happened to me.
I’m thankful that I get to know my creator and his only son, Jesus.
Because so many times in my life, I seek Him and I got the answer.
I knocked, and He opened the door for me.
Without His words, the words of the Bible, I wouldn’t be able to make it this far.
We need the words to lift us up mentally and spiritually and to get going.
Prayer and Bible.
Every morning when I wake up I thank God that I was able to live in this country.
Sometime it feels like a dream.
Living my life in this great country was something I can be thankful for everyday and brag about wherever I go.
I have more than enough.
Since I’m in this country, there was no more hunger, there were no more fears, there was no more persecution, and there was no more heartache.
I have a voice to speak up for myself.
I can worship my God without fear.
My voice finally matters.
