Love stories like this?
4 things that helped me become a better student in America
For an example, some of the schools in Tanzania do not provide lunch.
Students had to keep it up with the homework.
Students are forced to learn more than here.
There are a lot of ways that anybody especially foreigners can take to become successful in American schools.
First, respect.
You pay attention in class because you respect the teacher and work on what he/she gives you to do.
You must know why you are in school that will determine what you want to be.
Thirdly, commitment.
Commit to waking up every morning to go to school and study hard to accomplish your goals.
Taking notes will not only keep you more engaged during class, but will also help you narrow down what you need to study when exam time rolls around.
Another way to be successful in American Schools is Asking Question.
Asking for help from a teacher, a tutor or your friends is a surefire way to make sure you truly understand the material.
Don’t underestimate the importance of those eight hours of sleep every night.
