Is trust is a mental health issue?
Our thinking does not contain anything outside of our own experiences.
Some people have had bad experiences in their lives and this could prevent them from believing in themselves.
When people have had bad experiences in their lives they often have negative self-talk and use negative experiences to define themselves.
When we are born the trust between one’s heart and mind is as full as it can be, because no physical experience or an incident has taken place yet.
At this point, the trust between the heart and the mind functions the same way.
However, when that child puts its hand in the fire and gets burnt, it destroys the “original” trust that was there between the mind and the heart.
From there and on, the child grows up with a fear of fire because the child has had a practiced knowledge of what the fire can do.
Experience is a valuable thing whether bad or good.
When people have many bad experiences, it obviously takes longer for them to build trust between their mind and heart.
This is one of the reasons when people are heart-broken it can take forever to trust again or may never get rid of how they felt when that incident took place.
This is to say that being aware of this alone can help someone understand why he or she thinks the way he or she does.
When people have faced unfathomable circumstances in their lives that might cause trauma, the best way to help them is to understand where they are coming from.
It communicates to them that they are not alone and knowing that they are understood is the best way to start fresh.
