Wood can also swell or warp due to humidity and weather conditions. There is a higher likelihood of injury due to animals or insects with wood than with steel.
The cost of a steel warehouse over time is where steel begins to show out over other building materials. Steel is lightweight, strong, and not susceptible to most environmental problems.
What Does a 5000 Square Foot Warehouse Cost for Me?
The first thing you’ll need to consider is what kind of building you’re looking at getting. Do you need a fully-enclosed, finished metal structure or just a rigid-frame steel building that is open?
If you’re wanting a finished and enclosed building, those will run about $19-$28 per square foot. If your building is on the more complex end, these structures can run up to $40 per square foot, but that’s not as common.
Commercial steel buildings are right up the alley of a lot of banks, so bank financing is almost always an option for most buyers. If the bank won’t roll your building, you could think about a rent to own agreement .
But since you are renting to own, the current owner knows that you want to take it off his or her hands. The owner will often allow you to make special modifications or allow you to handle the building as if it were already yours.
Now you know all the basics of steel warehouses, the initial investment, the time saving, and the incredible low-maintenance power of steel.
