We have no changes to visa requirements to announce at this time. Information regarding required vaccinations for immigrant visa applicants may be found onthis website.
Q.3 There are reports of foreign nationals traveling to Florida to receive vaccines. Is that permitted under the law?
For questions regarding individuals' eligibility to receive the vaccine in the United States as part of a priority group, we refer you to local health authorities.
Q.4 What will happen to U.S. citizens or foreign nationals who present forged or otherwise illegitimate negative COVID test results in order to try to enter the United States? Per the CDC’s order, travelers must present a verifiable, documented test result to their airline in order to travel.
Q.6 If I'm vaccinated, do I have to present a negative COVID test to fly to the United States?
All passengers age two and older are subject to the order, even those who have received a COVID-19 vaccine. For questions regarding the testing requirements, we refer you to the CDC, which has information on Requirement for Proof of Negative COVID-19 Test or Recovery from COVID-19 for All Air Passengers Arriving in the United StatesandFrequently Asked Questions about COVID-19 Vaccination.
