If all these questions have crossed your mind from time to time, it is time to answer them.
Well, keep reading and you will know what we are talking about.
In other words, economic growth is an increase that occurs in the GDP or national income per person of a country in a certain period of time (normally one year). That is, if the money that each person has grows, it is said that there is greater economic growth.
For example, it can happen because new natural resources are discovered that allow supplying a greater number of people; because the number of workers who can produce more products is increased; or because there is a capital increase, which can be invested in the above, resources and workers.
It is not alone the fact of improving the productivity of machines and personnel, but above all in quality. If you produce products that are of better quality, the demand will be higher because people will trust those products over others.
The best years are said to have been from the end of World War II until the oil crisis in 1970. But there have been many other periods, before and after.
GDP, or its full name, Gross Domestic Product, can be understood as the market value of the production of goods and services in a country. In other words, it is what a product that a consumer buys is worth.
But it is also necessary to take into account the quality of life of each person and if it increases or decreases. For example, a country does not grow because it has 1000 billion euros if the income of each person decreases by 500 because there is more population, or other problems.
In an increasingly connected world where distances no longer become a problem and you can have clients and contacts with anyone anywhere in the world, networking has become a common practice for both entrepreneurs and the world of work. .
2 What goals do you have
Networking can be defined as the activity that involves an increase in the network of contacts of an entrepreneur. In other words, we are talking about building a network of contacts but with a specific objective: having more business and job opportunities.
What goals do you have Although we have told you before that the objective is to have job and business opportunities, the truth is that there is much more you can get from networking.
Create relationships with companies, suppliers, distributors, allies, potential customers ...
Actually, networking is a way to have a circle of people, companies, etc. that can help you at any given moment to publicize what you want to launch at a professional level.
Now that you know what networking is, you should know that there is not only one type, but two types are established:
offline, where you can get networking in the face-to-face events you attend, in conferences, workshops, courses, lectures, or even in the workplace (because you meet a person at work who can help you to make the leap to another company, for example). Now, to achieve this you need to have social skills and do not be shy to be able to relate.
It is always best to combine both, since online allows you to reach people who, otherwise, you would never meet or have contact; and offline you would have the facility to make yourself known and generate a good first impression. How to Network
Something that we could say is similar to the business card, and that works very well for online networking, is the elevator pitch. It is a presentation of no more than 2 minutes about you, your business, product, service or career and what you want to achieve.
When you carry out an economic activity, one of the procedures that you have to carry out is the installment payment on account of personal income tax. This is done through model 130.
Model 130 encompasses what is the "Quarterly income tax return for individuals". It is a payment that is made in installments (it is paid every three months) for which part of the payment that should be made from personal income tax is paid to the Treasury.
That they carry out economic activities, including those of agriculture, livestock, forestry or fishing. Of course, they have to establish the direct estimation method, either normal or simplified.
If they are civil partnerships and / or communities of property. In this case, each partner must make the payment based on their participation.
Now that it is clearer to you what form 130 is, it is time to know how you should fill it in so that it is good for the Treasury and does not attract your attention; or worse still, they impose a sanction on you.
However, when filling in form 130, you have to add the income you declared in the first quarter with that of the second. In other words, in this last quarter it would not be 200 euros of profit, but 300 euros (200 + 100 in the first quarter).
Section II, focused on those who carry out an agricultural, forestry, fishing or livestock activity, who will have to fill in the model in this part.
To make it clearer, keep the following in mind:
In other words. What you have to pay (box 4) will be deducted from the withholdings (5 and 6) that are already assumed to have been entered in your name.
Box 8: you must enter the income throughout the year, including grants, aid ...
Box 10: used to put the withholdings that you have had to apply on the invoices you have made.
Finally, Part III is the summary, and the corresponding boxes are:
Box 13: something that not many know is that, when your income is low, the Treasury allows you a reduction of up to 100 euros. The best thing is that you look for information about that specific box to know the value that you can apply to discount (if you can).
Box 15: used to record negative values. In other words, if you have had negative results in box 19, you must indicate it, in addition, you must bear in mind that the value of this box cannot be higher than that of 14.
In this way, you can have a guide and better understand what model 130 is and how to fill it in properly so that everything is correct.
Have you ever wondered why a country grows?
Why is the economy of a country causing growth or not?
For this, you have to understand the concept of economic growth, of the causes that cause it as well as its way of measuring. Do you want us to inform you about all this?
2.2 Economic growth caused by an increase in productivity
Now, it is not as easy as we are putting it in the example.
Now, in this way, China is the richest country in the world, but it is really not because every person is rich, but because there are millions of them. Therefore, when determining the growth of a country, there are several factors to take into account, because if we only limit ourselves to a few scales, the result may not be the most real (the case of China).
As a general rule, economic growth does not arise spontaneously, but is seen to come, except for sporadic cases. Taking into account that we are talking about an increase in production, there may be two reasons why this happens: that there are more production factors, that is, more quantity; or that the same thing is produced but with better quality.
In this case, economic growth would occur because there is a greater quantity of resources (material and / or human) that allow us to produce a greater quantity.
And this is achieved above all with an improvement in the technology that is used or with the training of workers, as well as their experience, which will make them know how to do their work much better.
And it is that this was the trigger for it to be seen that the countries were growing. According to Angus Maddison, a renowned economist, the growth in the last 40 years has been spectacular, not only at an economic level, but also in terms of population (which has multiplied by five), in income per person (which has multiplied by eight), or World GDP (multiplied by XNUMX).
There are many reasons for economic growth, from technological advancement to a greater accumulation of physical and human capital, opening up to foreign markets, etc. All this has allowed countries to develop and grow, some more than others, but all of them are richer when compared to other times.
